{0 Testing}

Use deterministic capture to test semantic logs without depending on console
layout, files, randomness, or global production delivery.

{[
let test_config =
  Observe.Config.create_exn ~service:"orders-test" ()

let captured =
  Lwt_main.run
    (Observe_lwt_unix.Test.with_capture_exn ~config:test_config (fun capture ->
       let open Lwt.Syntax in
       let* () = Checkout.run () in
       Lwt.return (Observe.Capture.logs capture)))
]}

Capture installs an isolated Lwt-local route for the callback, suppresses
production delivery, restores the previous route on return, exception, or
cancellation, and closes exactly once. It bypasses probabilistic retention and
external routing while preserving level admission, finite materialization, and
global redaction.

Inspect package meaning directly:

{[
let operation_name log =
  match Observe.Log.kind log with
  | Observe.Log.Point _ -> None
  | Observe.Log.Wide { operation; _ } ->
      Some (Observe.Log.operation_name operation)

let cart_id log =
  Option.bind
    (Observe.Value.find [ "cart_id" ] (Observe.Log.fields log))
    (fun value ->
      match Observe.Value.view value with
      | `String value -> Some value
      | _ -> None)
]}

Do not parse pretty or JSON output to assert domain meaning. Formatter snapshots
are appropriate only when the presentation itself is under test.

For deterministic operation identity and sampling, ready initialization accepts
[~id_generator] and [~sampling_draw]. The portable {!module:Observe.Make}
accepts a complete injected {!module-type:Observe.IO.S} for controlled clocks,
identity, sampling, dynamic scope, console behavior, and control exceptions.

The repository's correctness and stress profiles are documented in
[test/README.md].
